IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ica-dates`
IMPORT `ica-core`
IMPORT `ica-seat`

-- Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA), Parts 7A and 7B -- cases for the seat of the person abused as a child (ica-seat.l4).
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text (the section is named on each group), never copied
-- from the encoding's output; day counts are shown where they matter. Edges: the 18th year (17 and 18), 31 July and
-- 1 August 2022 (Divisions 2 and 3; s 50U; s 50V(1)(b)), 31 January and 1 February 2019 (s 50V(1)(a)), the 119th and
-- 120th day after commencing (s 50J(6)(a)), the 28th and 29th day after the order (s 50J(7)(a)), a leap-year February,
-- and every open list ("includes") against a closed one ("means").
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases: the person abused as a child`

-- Short names for the inputs.
`SEX` MEANS `sexual abuse`
`SPHYS` MEANS `serious physical abuse`
`PSYREL` MEANS `psychological abuse related to sexual abuse or serious physical abuse`
`PHYS` MEANS `physical abuse that was not serious`
`PSYOTHER` MEANS `psychological abuse not related to sexual abuse or serious physical abuse`

`EMP` MEANS `an officer, office holder, representative, leader, owner, employee, agent, volunteer or contractor of the institution`
`MIN` MEANS `a minister of religion, religious leader or member of the personnel of the institution, a religious organisation`
`DELIND` MEANS `the individual to whom the institution delegated the care, supervision, control or authority over me`
`DELSTAFF` MEANS `an officer, office holder, representative, leader, owner, employee, agent, volunteer or contractor of the entity to which the institution delegated my care`
`CARER` MEANS `a designated carer with whom I was placed, not my parent or guardian`
`CARERPARENT` MEANS `a designated carer with whom I was placed, who was my parent or guardian`
`FUNDED` MEANS `a person associated only with an entity that the institution funds or regulates`
`OTHERCONN` MEANS `some other connection`

`FOUND` MEANS `the court has found that it is so`
`NOTFOUND` MEANS `the court has found that it is not so`
`UNDECIDED` MEANS `the court has not decided yet`

§§ `s 50A, s 50C -- is it an abuse claim`

`AC_YES` MEANS `yes: an abuse claim, a claim arising from the abuse of a child by a person associated with an institution while the child was under its care, supervision, control or authority (s 50A(1))`
`AC_ADULT` MEANS `no: "child" means a person under 18 years of age (s 50A(1)), and you were 18 or over`
`AC_NOINST` MEANS `no: an institution means an entity, private or public, that is responsible for a child and provides an activity, program or service giving a person an opportunity for contact with a child (s 50A(1), "institution" (a))`
`AC_FAMILY` MEANS `no: an institution does not include a family (s 50A(1), "institution" (b))`
`AC_NOCARE` MEANS `no: an abuse claim needs the abuse to have happened while you were under the institution's care, supervision, control or authority (s 50A(1))`
`AC_FUNDED` MEANS `no: a person is not associated with an institution only because they are associated with an entity the institution funds or regulates (s 50C(2))`
`AC_KINDOPEN` MEANS `the Act does not say: abuse "includes" sexual abuse, serious physical abuse and psychological abuse related to them (s 50A(1)), and the list is not closed`
`AC_CONNOPEN` MEANS `the Act does not say: the persons associated with an institution "include" those listed in s 50C(1), and the list is not closed`

-- A teacher (employee) sexually abused a pupil of 12 at school: every element of s 50A holds.
#ASSERT `Is my claim an abuse claim against an institution` 12 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `EMP` TRUE EQUALS `AC_YES`
-- 17 is still a child; 18 is not.
#ASSERT `Is my claim an abuse claim against an institution` 17 `SPHYS` TRUE FALSE `EMP` TRUE EQUALS `AC_YES`
#ASSERT `Is my claim an abuse claim against an institution` 18 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `EMP` TRUE EQUALS `AC_ADULT`
-- Each of the three listed kinds.
#ASSERT `Is my claim an abuse claim against an institution` 9 `PSYREL` TRUE FALSE `EMP` TRUE EQUALS `AC_YES`
-- Each listed connection in s 50C(1)(a)-(d).
#ASSERT `Is my claim an abuse claim against an institution` 11 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `MIN` TRUE EQUALS `AC_YES`
#ASSERT `Is my claim an abuse claim against an institution` 11 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `DELIND` TRUE EQUALS `AC_YES`
#ASSERT `Is my claim an abuse claim against an institution` 11 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `DELSTAFF` TRUE EQUALS `AC_YES`
#ASSERT `Is my claim an abuse claim against an institution` 11 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `CARER` TRUE EQUALS `AC_YES`
-- "institution" means (a) ... and (b) not a family: closed.
#ASSERT `Is my claim an abuse claim against an institution` 11 `SEX` FALSE FALSE `EMP` TRUE EQUALS `AC_NOINST`
#ASSERT `Is my claim an abuse claim against an institution` 11 `SEX` TRUE TRUE `EMP` TRUE EQUALS `AC_FAMILY`
-- Not in the institution's care when abused.
#ASSERT `Is my claim an abuse claim against an institution` 11 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `EMP` FALSE EQUALS `AC_NOCARE`
-- s 50C(2): association only through a funded or regulated entity is a flat no, even with an unlisted kind.
#ASSERT `Is my claim an abuse claim against an institution` 11 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `FUNDED` TRUE EQUALS `AC_FUNDED`
#ASSERT `Is my claim an abuse claim against an institution` 11 `PHYS` TRUE FALSE `FUNDED` TRUE EQUALS `AC_FUNDED`
-- Open lists: physical abuse that was not serious, unrelated psychological abuse, another kind; a parent who is the
-- designated carer (fork F3); some other connection.
#ASSERT `Is my claim an abuse claim against an institution` 11 `PHYS` TRUE FALSE `EMP` TRUE EQUALS `AC_KINDOPEN`
#ASSERT `Is my claim an abuse claim against an institution` 11 `PSYOTHER` TRUE FALSE `EMP` TRUE EQUALS `AC_KINDOPEN`
#ASSERT `Is my claim an abuse claim against an institution` 11 `another kind of abuse` TRUE FALSE `EMP` TRUE EQUALS `AC_KINDOPEN`
#ASSERT `Is my claim an abuse claim against an institution` 11 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `CARERPARENT` TRUE EQUALS `AC_CONNOPEN`
#ASSERT `Is my claim an abuse claim against an institution` 11 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `OTHERCONN` TRUE EQUALS `AC_CONNOPEN`
-- Both open: the kind is named first.
#ASSERT `Is my claim an abuse claim against an institution` 11 `PHYS` TRUE FALSE `OTHERCONN` TRUE EQUALS `AC_KINDOPEN`
-- A "no" settles it before an open list: 18 years old with an unlisted kind.
#ASSERT `Is my claim an abuse claim against an institution` 18 `PHYS` TRUE FALSE `OTHERCONN` TRUE EQUALS `AC_ADULT`

§§ `s 50A(1), (2) -- employee, and akin to an employee`

`EM_YES` MEANS `yes: an employee of the institution`
`EM_AKIN` MEANS `yes: akin to an employee, and so an employee of the institution for Part 7A (s 50A(1), (2))`
`EM_INDEP` MEANS `no: not akin to an employee, because the activities were carried out for a recognisably independent business (s 50A(2)(a))`
`EM_CARER` MEANS `no: not akin to an employee, because the activities were those of a designated carer, carried on as a designated carer (s 50A(2)(b))`
`EM_NO` MEANS `no: not an employee, and not akin to one, which needs activities carried out as an integral part of the institution's activities and for its benefit (s 50A(2))`

#ASSERT `Was the person who abused me an employee of the institution` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `EM_YES`
-- The s 50A(2) exceptions qualify "akin" only; an employee is an employee.
#ASSERT `Was the person who abused me an employee of the institution` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `EM_YES`
-- A priest who is not employed but whose ministry is integral to the church and for its benefit.
#ASSERT `Was the person who abused me an employee of the institution` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `EM_AKIN`
#ASSERT `Was the person who abused me an employee of the institution` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `EM_INDEP`
#ASSERT `Was the person who abused me an employee of the institution` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `EM_CARER`
#ASSERT `Was the person who abused me an employee of the institution` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `EM_NO`
#ASSERT `Was the person who abused me an employee of the institution` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `EM_NO`

§§ `ss 50D, 50E, 50F -- the duty and the reversed onus`

`DU_YES` MEANS `yes: the institution is taken to have breached its duty to take all reasonable steps to prevent the abuse, because it has not proved that it took them (ss 50E(1), 50F(2))`
`DU_PROVED` MEANS `no: the institution proved that it took all reasonable steps to prevent the abuse, so it is not taken to have breached its duty (s 50F(2))`
`DU_UNLESS` MEANS `yes, unless the institution proves that it took all reasonable steps to prevent the abuse (s 50F(2)); the court weighs the matters in s 50F(3)`
`DU_UNRELATED` MEANS `no: the duty does not apply to abuse in circumstances wholly unrelated to the abuser's association with the institution (s 50E(2))`
`DU_DELEGATE` MEANS `no: your care was delegated to another institution, and the duty does not apply to abuse by a person associated with the delegate in circumstances wholly unrelated to that person's association with either institution (s 50E(3))`
`DU_BEFORE` MEANS `Division 2 does not reach this on its words: s 50D(1) applies Part 7A to causes of action that arose before 1 August 2022 but leaves Divisions 2 and 3 out; the general law of negligence still applies`
`DU_NOTCLAIM` MEANS `Division 2 does not reach this: on these facts the claim is not an abuse claim (see the abuse claim question)`
`DU_OPEN` MEANS `the Act does not say: whether this is an abuse claim turns on an open list in s 50A or s 50C (see the abuse claim question)`

-- Abuse on 1 August 2022, the day Part 7A came into operation: Division 2 reaches it.
#ASSERT `Is the institution taken to have breached its duty to prevent the abuse` 13 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `EMP` TRUE (`the date` 1 8 2022) FALSE FALSE FALSE `UNDECIDED` EQUALS `DU_UNLESS`
-- The day before: Division 2 does not reach it on its words (finding 1).
#ASSERT `Is the institution taken to have breached its duty to prevent the abuse` 13 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `EMP` TRUE (`the date` 31 7 2022) FALSE FALSE FALSE `NOTFOUND` EQUALS `DU_BEFORE`
#ASSERT `Is the institution taken to have breached its duty to prevent the abuse` 13 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `EMP` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) FALSE FALSE FALSE `NOTFOUND` EQUALS `DU_YES`
#ASSERT `Is the institution taken to have breached its duty to prevent the abuse` 13 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `EMP` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) FALSE FALSE FALSE `FOUND` EQUALS `DU_PROVED`
-- s 50E(2): wholly unrelated to the association.
#ASSERT `Is the institution taken to have breached its duty to prevent the abuse` 13 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `EMP` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) TRUE FALSE FALSE `NOTFOUND` EQUALS `DU_UNRELATED`
-- s 50E(3): delegated, and wholly unrelated to the association with either institution; then not unrelated.
#ASSERT `Is the institution taken to have breached its duty to prevent the abuse` 13 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `DELSTAFF` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) FALSE TRUE TRUE `NOTFOUND` EQUALS `DU_DELEGATE`
#ASSERT `Is the institution taken to have breached its duty to prevent the abuse` 13 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `DELSTAFF` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) FALSE TRUE FALSE `UNDECIDED` EQUALS `DU_UNLESS`
-- Not an abuse claim (18 years old), and an open list (a parent as designated carer).
#ASSERT `Is the institution taken to have breached its duty to prevent the abuse` 18 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `EMP` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) FALSE FALSE FALSE `NOTFOUND` EQUALS `DU_NOTCLAIM`
#ASSERT `Is the institution taken to have breached its duty to prevent the abuse` 13 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `CARERPARENT` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) FALSE FALSE FALSE `NOTFOUND` EQUALS `DU_OPEN`

§§ `ss 50D, 50G -- vicarious liability`

`VI_YES` MEANS `yes: the institution is vicariously liable for the abuse (s 50G(1)), in addition to any liability at common law (s 50G(3))`
`VI_IF` MEANS `yes, if the court finds that the apparent performance of the role in which the institution placed the employee supplied the occasion for the abuse (s 50G(1)(a)); it takes into account whether the role gave the employee authority, power or control over you, your trust, or the ability to achieve intimacy with you (s 50G(2))`
`VI_NOTEMP` MEANS `no: s 50G makes an institution vicariously liable only for abuse by an employee, or a person akin to one (s 50G(1), s 50A(2)); the common law still applies (s 50G(3))`
`VI_NOCARE` MEANS `no: s 50G needs the abuse to have happened while you were under the institution's care, supervision, control or authority (s 50G(1)(c)); the common law still applies (s 50G(3))`
`VI_NOADV` MEANS `no: s 50G needs the employee to have taken advantage of the occasion the role supplied (s 50G(1)(b)); the common law still applies (s 50G(3))`
`VI_NOOCC` MEANS `no: the court found that the role did not supply the occasion for the abuse (s 50G(1)(a)); the common law still applies (s 50G(3))`
`VI_ADULT` MEANS `no: s 50G covers the abuse of a child, a person under 18 (s 50A(1))`
`VI_NOINST` MEANS `no: s 50G makes an institution liable, and an institution means an entity responsible for a child that provides an activity, program or service giving contact with children, and not a family (s 50A(1))`
`VI_BEFORE` MEANS `Division 3 does not reach this on its words: s 50D(1) applies Part 7A to causes of action that arose before 1 August 2022 but leaves Divisions 2 and 3 out; the common law of vicarious liability still applies`
`VI_OPEN` MEANS `the Act does not say whether s 50G reaches this: abuse "includes" sexual abuse, serious physical abuse and psychological abuse related to them (s 50A(1)), and the list is not closed`

-- A youth worker employed by a club, alone with a 14-year-old on a camp in March 2024.
#ASSERT `Is the institution vicariously liable for the abuse by its employee` 14 `SEX` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `UNDECIDED` TRUE EQUALS `VI_IF`
#ASSERT `Is the institution vicariously liable for the abuse by its employee` 14 `SEX` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `FOUND` TRUE EQUALS `VI_YES`
#ASSERT `Is the institution vicariously liable for the abuse by its employee` 14 `SEX` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `NOTFOUND` TRUE EQUALS `VI_NOOCC`
#ASSERT `Is the institution vicariously liable for the abuse by its employee` 14 `SEX` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `FOUND` FALSE EQUALS `VI_NOADV`
#ASSERT `Is the institution vicariously liable for the abuse by its employee` 14 `SEX` TRUE FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 3 2024) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `FOUND` TRUE EQUALS `VI_NOCARE`
-- A volunteer akin to an employee counts; a contractor with an independent business does not.
#ASSERT `Is the institution vicariously liable for the abuse by its employee` 14 `SEX` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `FOUND` TRUE EQUALS `VI_YES`
#ASSERT `Is the institution vicariously liable for the abuse by its employee` 14 `SEX` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `FOUND` TRUE EQUALS `VI_NOTEMP`
-- 31 July 2022 and 1 August 2022.
#ASSERT `Is the institution vicariously liable for the abuse by its employee` 14 `SEX` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`the date` 31 7 2022) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `FOUND` TRUE EQUALS `VI_BEFORE`
#ASSERT `Is the institution vicariously liable for the abuse by its employee` 14 `SEX` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`the date` 1 8 2022) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `FOUND` TRUE EQUALS `VI_YES`
#ASSERT `Is the institution vicariously liable for the abuse by its employee` 18 `SEX` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `FOUND` TRUE EQUALS `VI_ADULT`
#ASSERT `Is the institution vicariously liable for the abuse by its employee` 14 `SEX` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `FOUND` TRUE EQUALS `VI_NOINST`
-- An unlisted kind: open, unless the court has already found against the occasion.
#ASSERT `Is the institution vicariously liable for the abuse by its employee` 14 `PHYS` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `FOUND` TRUE EQUALS `VI_OPEN`
#ASSERT `Is the institution vicariously liable for the abuse by its employee` 14 `PHYS` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `NOTFOUND` TRUE EQUALS `VI_NOOCC`

§§ `ss 50H-50K, 50S -- whom to sue`

`R_CORP` MEANS `the institution itself, which was already incorporated when the cause of action accrued: Division 4 does not reach this, and the ordinary law applies`
`R_50H_OH` MEANS `the institution, now incorporated, in place of the former office holder: it takes over their liability, acts, duties, defences and right to indemnity (s 50H(2), (3))`
`R_50H_INST` MEANS `the institution, now incorporated, on the claim that lay against it while it was unincorporated (s 50H(1)(b)(ii), (2))`
`R_50H_NONE` MEANS `no route under s 50H: it applies only if you could maintain the proceedings had nothing changed (s 50H(1)(e))`
`R_50I` MEANS `the current holder of the office of authority, in the name of the office, in place of the former office holder (s 50I(2), (3)); if no office is substantially the same, the current head of the institution (s 50S(3))`
`R_50J` MEANS `the unincorporated institution itself, with notice of the claim to its head as the regulations require (s 50J(2), (3))`
`R_50K` MEANS `the institution's nominee, which takes on the institution's liability, while the institution must still take part (s 50K)`

#ASSERT `Whom can I bring my abuse claim against` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (LIST `R_CORP`)
-- An unincorporated church, since incorporated; the claim is founded on a former bishop's responsibility.
#ASSERT `Whom can I bring my abuse claim against` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (LIST `R_50H_OH`)
#ASSERT `Whom can I bring my abuse claim against` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (LIST `R_50H_INST`)
#ASSERT `Whom can I bring my abuse claim against` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (LIST `R_50H_NONE`)
-- Unincorporated then and now.
#ASSERT `Whom can I bring my abuse claim against` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (LIST `R_50J`)
#ASSERT `Whom can I bring my abuse claim against` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (LIST `R_50J`, `R_50I`, `R_50K`)
-- The former office holder still holds the office: s 50I does not apply (s 50I(1)(e)).
#ASSERT `Whom can I bring my abuse claim against` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (LIST `R_50J`)
-- Could not maintain the proceedings even had the office holder stayed (s 50I(1)(f)).
#ASSERT `Whom can I bring my abuse claim against` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (LIST `R_50J`)
#ASSERT `Whom can I bring my abuse claim against` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (LIST `R_50J`, `R_50K`)

§§ `s 50R -- continuity`

`CO_SAME` MEANS `yes: today's institution is the same institution, as the class or type of its members and its primary purposes or work are substantially the same (s 50R(1), (2)), whatever changed in its name, structure, incorporation or area (s 50R(3))`
`CO_IF` MEANS `yes, if the court finds today's institution substantially the same as it was when the cause of action accrued (s 50R(1)); the sufficient test of s 50R(2) is not met on these facts`
`CO_SUCC` MEANS `yes: today's institution is a relevant successor of the old institution, and is taken to be the same institution (s 50R(4), (5))`
`CO_JOINT` MEANS `yes: each of the relevant successors is jointly and severally liable for the abuse, and each may recover contribution from the others (s 50R(6))`
`CO_NONE` MEANS `the Act does not say: with no institution the same or substantially the same, and no relevant successor, s 50R names no one`

#ASSERT `Is today's institution the one that is liable` `it continues, perhaps with a new name, structure, incorporation or area` TRUE TRUE 0 EQUALS `CO_SAME`
#ASSERT `Is today's institution the one that is liable` `it continues, perhaps with a new name, structure, incorporation or area` TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS `CO_IF`
#ASSERT `Is today's institution the one that is liable` `all or part of it merged into another institution` FALSE FALSE 1 EQUALS `CO_SUCC`
#ASSERT `Is today's institution the one that is liable` `all or part of it merged with other entities to form a new institution` FALSE FALSE 2 EQUALS `CO_JOINT`
#ASSERT `Is today's institution the one that is liable` `part of it left, and the remainder continues as an institution` FALSE TRUE 1 EQUALS `CO_SUCC`
#ASSERT `Is today's institution the one that is liable` `a chain of such mergers, remainders and continuations leads to today's institution` FALSE FALSE 1 EQUALS `CO_SUCC`
#ASSERT `Is today's institution the one that is liable` `it ceased, with no successor` FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `CO_NONE`

§§ `s 50U -- an earlier judgment that the defendant was not appropriate`

`EJ_YES` MEANS `yes: the court has granted leave, being satisfied that it is just and reasonable (s 50U(2))`
`EJ_LEAVE` MEANS `not without leave: you may commence the proceedings only if a court, satisfied that it is just and reasonable, grants leave (s 50U(1), (2))`
`EJ_REFUSED` MEANS `no: the court did not grant leave, and the proceedings may only be commenced with it (s 50U(2))`
`EJ_AFTER` MEANS `no: s 50U covers only a judgment given before 1 August 2022, when Part 7A came into operation (s 50U(1))`
`EJ_NONE` MEANS `s 50U does not arise: there was no earlier judgment that the defendant was not an appropriate defendant`

#ASSERT `Can I sue again after an earlier judgment that the defendant was not appropriate` FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) `UNDECIDED` EQUALS `EJ_NONE`
#ASSERT `Can I sue again after an earlier judgment that the defendant was not appropriate` TRUE (`the date` 31 7 2022) `UNDECIDED` EQUALS `EJ_LEAVE`
#ASSERT `Can I sue again after an earlier judgment that the defendant was not appropriate` TRUE (`the date` 1 8 2022) `FOUND` EQUALS `EJ_AFTER`
#ASSERT `Can I sue again after an earlier judgment that the defendant was not appropriate` TRUE (`the date` 15 6 2005) `FOUND` EQUALS `EJ_YES`
#ASSERT `Can I sue again after an earlier judgment that the defendant was not appropriate` TRUE (`the date` 15 6 2005) `NOTFOUND` EQUALS `EJ_REFUSED`

§§ `s 50B -- associated trusts`

`TR_YES` MEANS `yes: an associated trust of the institution (s 50B(1))`
`TR_ORDER` MEANS `yes, for Divisions 5 and 6 (paying an abuse claim): a court order under s 50J(5) is in force for it (s 50B(2))`
`TR_NOUSE` MEANS `no: a trust is an associated trust only if the institution uses it to carry out its functions or activities (s 50B(1))`
`TR_NOPOWER` MEANS `no: the institution uses the trust, but neither it nor a member or manager has a power over the trust listed in s 50B(1)(a), and the trustee does not act on their directions (s 50B(1)(c))`

#ASSERT `Is this trust an associated trust of the institution` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `TR_YES`
#ASSERT `Is this trust an associated trust of the institution` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `TR_YES`
#ASSERT `Is this trust an associated trust of the institution` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `TR_YES`
#ASSERT `Is this trust an associated trust of the institution` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `TR_NOPOWER`
#ASSERT `Is this trust an associated trust of the institution` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `TR_NOUSE`
#ASSERT `Is this trust an associated trust of the institution` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `TR_ORDER`
#ASSERT `Is this trust an associated trust of the institution` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `TR_ORDER`

§§ `ss 50L-50P -- out of what a judgment may be paid`

#ASSERT `Out of what assets can my judgment or settlement be paid` `the institution` EQUALS (LIST `the institution's assets`, `the assets of an associated trust of the institution`)
#ASSERT `Out of what assets can my judgment or settlement be paid` `the institution's nominee, which is the trustee of an associated trust of the institution` EQUALS (LIST `the assets of the trust of which the nominee is trustee, the trustee being liable only up to the value of the trust property (ss 50M(2), 50O(4))`, `the institution's assets`)
#ASSERT `Out of what assets can my judgment or settlement be paid` `the institution's nominee, which is not the trustee of an associated trust` EQUALS (LIST `the nominee's own assets`, `the institution's assets`)
#ASSERT `Out of what assets can my judgment or settlement be paid` `the current office holder, sued in the name of the office` EQUALS (LIST `the institution's assets`, `the assets of an associated trust of the institution`, `not the current office holder's own assets: they are not personally liable (s 50N(2))`)

§§ `s 50J(5), (6) -- a trustee as nominee`

`NO_INC` MEANS `no: s 50J applies only to an institution that is an unincorporated body (s 50J(1))`
`NO_NOMINEE` MEANS `no: there is a nominee, and the court is not satisfied that it lacks sufficient assets to meet the claim (s 50J(6)(b))`
`NO_NEVER` MEANS `no: the trust is not, and never was, an associated trust of the institution (s 50J(5)(a))`
`NO_CEASED` MEANS `no: the trust is no longer an associated trust, and the court is not satisfied that a reason it ceased was to keep its property from meeting an abuse claim (s 50J(5)(b))`
`NO_APPROP` MEANS `no: the court is not satisfied that the order would be appropriate (s 50J(5)(c))`
`NO_YES` MEANS `yes: the court is satisfied of everything s 50J(5) and (6) need, and may order that the trustee is the institution's nominee (s 50J(5))`
`NO_MAY` MEANS `yes, you may apply: the court may order that the trustee is the institution's nominee if it is satisfied of the matters still to be decided in s 50J(5) and (6)(b)(ii)`

-- Commenced 1 March 2024. 120 days: March 1 to 31 is 30, to 30 April 60, to 31 May 91, to 29 June 120. So the 120
-- days have passed on 29 June 2024; on 28 June (119 days) not yet.
#ASSERT `Can I ask the court to make a trust's trustee the institution's nominee` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) (`the date` 28 6 2024) FALSE `UNDECIDED` TRUE FALSE `UNDECIDED` `FOUND` EQUALS (`not yet: s 50J(5) applies once at least 120 days have passed since the proceeding was commenced (s 50J(6)(a)); they will have passed on` (`the date` 29 6 2024))
#ASSERT `Can I ask the court to make a trust's trustee the institution's nominee` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) (`the date` 29 6 2024) FALSE `UNDECIDED` TRUE FALSE `UNDECIDED` `FOUND` EQUALS `NO_YES`
#ASSERT `Can I ask the court to make a trust's trustee the institution's nominee` FALSE (`the date` 1 3 2024) (`the date` 29 6 2024) FALSE `UNDECIDED` TRUE FALSE `UNDECIDED` `FOUND` EQUALS `NO_INC`
-- A nominee exists: the court is not satisfied it lacks assets; then not yet decided.
#ASSERT `Can I ask the court to make a trust's trustee the institution's nominee` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) (`the date` 1 9 2024) TRUE `NOTFOUND` TRUE FALSE `UNDECIDED` `FOUND` EQUALS `NO_NOMINEE`
#ASSERT `Can I ask the court to make a trust's trustee the institution's nominee` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) (`the date` 1 9 2024) TRUE `UNDECIDED` TRUE FALSE `UNDECIDED` `FOUND` EQUALS `NO_MAY`
#ASSERT `Can I ask the court to make a trust's trustee the institution's nominee` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) (`the date` 1 9 2024) TRUE `FOUND` TRUE FALSE `UNDECIDED` `FOUND` EQUALS `NO_YES`
#ASSERT `Can I ask the court to make a trust's trustee the institution's nominee` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) (`the date` 1 9 2024) FALSE `UNDECIDED` FALSE FALSE `FOUND` `FOUND` EQUALS `NO_NEVER`
-- A trust that ceased to be associated: avoidance refused, found, undecided.
#ASSERT `Can I ask the court to make a trust's trustee the institution's nominee` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) (`the date` 1 9 2024) FALSE `UNDECIDED` FALSE TRUE `NOTFOUND` `FOUND` EQUALS `NO_CEASED`
#ASSERT `Can I ask the court to make a trust's trustee the institution's nominee` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) (`the date` 1 9 2024) FALSE `UNDECIDED` FALSE TRUE `FOUND` `FOUND` EQUALS `NO_YES`
#ASSERT `Can I ask the court to make a trust's trustee the institution's nominee` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) (`the date` 1 9 2024) FALSE `UNDECIDED` FALSE TRUE `UNDECIDED` `FOUND` EQUALS `NO_MAY`
#ASSERT `Can I ask the court to make a trust's trustee the institution's nominee` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) (`the date` 1 9 2024) FALSE `UNDECIDED` TRUE FALSE `UNDECIDED` `NOTFOUND` EQUALS `NO_APPROP`
#ASSERT `Can I ask the court to make a trust's trustee the institution's nominee` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2024) (`the date` 1 9 2024) FALSE `UNDECIDED` TRUE FALSE `UNDECIDED` `UNDECIDED` EQUALS `NO_MAY`

§§ `s 50J(7)(a) -- the order to identify associated trusts`

-- Order 1 March 2024, 28 days: the last day is 29 March 2024 (2 to 29 March is 28 days, 2024 a leap year does not
-- matter here). An order on 31 January 2023: 28 days later is 28 February 2023. 14 days from 1 March 2024: 15 March.
#ASSERT `By when must the institution identify its associated trusts` (`the date` 1 3 2024) FALSE 0 EQUALS (`the date` 29 3 2024)
#ASSERT `By when must the institution identify its associated trusts` (`the date` 31 1 2023) FALSE 0 EQUALS (`the date` 28 2 2023)
#ASSERT `By when must the institution identify its associated trusts` (`the date` 1 2 2024) FALSE 0 EQUALS (`the date` 29 2 2024)
#ASSERT `By when must the institution identify its associated trusts` (`the date` 1 3 2024) TRUE 14 EQUALS (`the date` 15 3 2024)

`OK` MEANS `in time: the institution complied on or before the last day`
`LATE` MEANS `late: the institution complied after the last day`
`WAITING` MEANS `still in time: the institution has not complied yet, and the last day has not passed`
`OVERDUE` MEANS `late: the institution has not complied, and the last day has passed`

#ASSERT `Has the institution identified its associated trusts in time` (`the date` 1 3 2024) FALSE 0 TRUE (`the date` 29 3 2024) (`the date` 1 5 2024) EQUALS `OK`
#ASSERT `Has the institution identified its associated trusts in time` (`the date` 1 3 2024) FALSE 0 TRUE (`the date` 30 3 2024) (`the date` 1 5 2024) EQUALS `LATE`
#ASSERT `Has the institution identified its associated trusts in time` (`the date` 1 3 2024) FALSE 0 TRUE (`the date` 2 3 2024) (`the date` 1 5 2024) EQUALS `OK`
#ASSERT `Has the institution identified its associated trusts in time` (`the date` 1 3 2024) FALSE 0 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 29 3 2024) EQUALS `WAITING`
#ASSERT `Has the institution identified its associated trusts in time` (`the date` 1 3 2024) FALSE 0 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 30 3 2024) EQUALS `OVERDUE`
#ASSERT `Has the institution identified its associated trusts in time` (`the date` 1 3 2024) TRUE 14 TRUE (`the date` 15 3 2024) (`the date` 1 5 2024) EQUALS `OK`
#ASSERT `Has the institution identified its associated trusts in time` (`the date` 1 3 2024) TRUE 14 TRUE (`the date` 16 3 2024) (`the date` 1 5 2024) EQUALS `LATE`

§§ `Part 7B, s 50V -- affected agreements`

`AA_BOTH` MEANS `yes: an affected agreement on both grounds (s 50V(1)(a) and (b))`
`AA_A` MEANS `yes: an affected agreement, made before 1 February 2019 when a limitation period on your claim for child abuse had already expired (s 50V(1)(a), (2))`
`AA_B` MEANS `yes: an affected agreement, made before 1 August 2022 when no one who would have been liable under Part 7A could be sued (s 50V(1)(b))`
`AA_NOBAR` MEANS `no: an affected agreement is one that prevents you from commencing or maintaining proceedings on the claim (s 50V(1))`
`AA_NO` MEANS `no: not an affected agreement, as it meets neither s 50V(1)(a) (made before 1 February 2019 on a child abuse claim whose limitation period had expired) nor s 50V(1)(b) (made before 1 August 2022 on an abuse claim when no one liable under Part 7A could be sued)`
`AA_OPEN` MEANS `the Act does not say: whether it is an affected agreement turns on an open list of what abuse, or who is associated with an institution, includes (s 3A(5) of the Limitation of Actions Act 1936; ss 50A, 50C)`

-- Abused at 10 by a church's minister; settled in 2010 for a small sum when time had run out and the unincorporated
-- church had no proper defendant: both limbs.
#ASSERT `Is my earlier settlement an affected agreement` 10 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `MIN` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 6 2010) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `AA_BOTH`
#ASSERT `Is my earlier settlement an affected agreement` 10 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `MIN` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 6 2010) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `AA_A`
#ASSERT `Is my earlier settlement an affected agreement` 10 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `MIN` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 6 2010) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `AA_B`
-- 31 January 2019 and 1 February 2019 (limb (a)).
#ASSERT `Is my earlier settlement an affected agreement` 10 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `MIN` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 31 1 2019) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `AA_A`
#ASSERT `Is my earlier settlement an affected agreement` 10 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `MIN` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 2 2019) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `AA_NO`
#ASSERT `Is my earlier settlement an affected agreement` 10 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `MIN` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 2 2019) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `AA_B`
-- 31 July 2022 and 1 August 2022 (limb (b)).
#ASSERT `Is my earlier settlement an affected agreement` 10 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `MIN` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 31 7 2022) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `AA_B`
#ASSERT `Is my earlier settlement an affected agreement` 10 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `MIN` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 8 2022) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `AA_NO`
-- It does not prevent proceedings.
#ASSERT `Is my earlier settlement an affected agreement` 10 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `MIN` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`the date` 1 6 2010) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `AA_NOBAR`
-- Abused at 18: neither limb.
#ASSERT `Is my earlier settlement an affected agreement` 18 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `MIN` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 6 2010) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `AA_NO`
-- Abused by a person with no institution behind them: limb (a) only (s 3A has no institution test).
#ASSERT `Is my earlier settlement an affected agreement` 10 `SEX` FALSE FALSE `OTHERCONN` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 6 2010) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `AA_A`
-- Physical abuse that was not serious: both limbs turn on an open list.
#ASSERT `Is my earlier settlement an affected agreement` 10 `PHYS` TRUE FALSE `EMP` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 6 2010) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `AA_OPEN`
#ASSERT `Is my earlier settlement an affected agreement` 10 `PHYS` TRUE FALSE `EMP` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 6 2010) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `AA_OPEN`
-- Physical abuse that was not serious, time not run out, a defendant available: no on both limbs.
#ASSERT `Is my earlier settlement an affected agreement` 10 `PHYS` TRUE FALSE `EMP` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 6 2010) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `AA_NO`
-- A parent as designated carer: limb (b) open, limb (a) fails (time had not run out).
#ASSERT `Is my earlier settlement an affected agreement` 10 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `CARERPARENT` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 6 2010) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `AA_OPEN`
-- Not a personal injury claim: limb (a) fails (s 3A is for death or personal injury), limb (b) holds.
#ASSERT `Is my earlier settlement an affected agreement` 10 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `MIN` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`the date` 1 6 2010) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `AA_B`

§§ `s 50W -- setting aside`

`SA_YES` MEANS `yes: the court has found it just and reasonable, and may set the agreement aside (s 50W(2)), with any contract, deed, order or judgment giving effect to it (s 50W(5))`
`SA_IF` MEANS `yes, if the court finds it just and reasonable: commence proceedings on the claim in a court with jurisdiction and apply to set the agreement aside (s 50W(1), (2)); the court may weigh the matters in s 50W(3), and the settlement negotiations may be put in evidence (s 50W(4))`
`SA_REFUSED` MEANS `no: the court may set an affected agreement aside only if it is just and reasonable, and it found that it is not (s 50W(2))`
`SA_REDRESS` MEANS `no: the court must not set aside a deed of release accepting an offer under the National Redress Scheme, or an agreement about a prior payment taken into account in that offer (s 50W(6)(a))`
`SA_INSURANCE` MEANS `no: the court must not set aside a contract of insurance (s 50W(6)(b))`
`SA_NOTAA` MEANS `no: Part 7B sets aside only an affected agreement (ss 50V, 50W(1)); see the affected agreement question`
`SA_OPEN` MEANS `the Act does not say whether this is an affected agreement (see the affected agreement question)`

#ASSERT `Can the court set aside my earlier settlement` 10 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `MIN` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 6 2010) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `UNDECIDED` EQUALS `SA_IF`
#ASSERT `Can the court set aside my earlier settlement` 10 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `MIN` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 6 2010) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `FOUND` EQUALS `SA_YES`
#ASSERT `Can the court set aside my earlier settlement` 10 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `MIN` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 6 2010) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `NOTFOUND` EQUALS `SA_REFUSED`
#ASSERT `Can the court set aside my earlier settlement` 10 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `MIN` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 6 2010) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `FOUND` EQUALS `SA_REDRESS`
#ASSERT `Can the court set aside my earlier settlement` 10 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `MIN` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 6 2010) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `FOUND` EQUALS `SA_INSURANCE`
#ASSERT `Can the court set aside my earlier settlement` 10 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `MIN` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 6 2010) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `FOUND` EQUALS `SA_REDRESS`
#ASSERT `Can the court set aside my earlier settlement` 10 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `MIN` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`the date` 1 6 2010) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `FOUND` EQUALS `SA_NOTAA`
#ASSERT `Can the court set aside my earlier settlement` 10 `SEX` TRUE FALSE `MIN` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 8 2022) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `FOUND` EQUALS `SA_NOTAA`
#ASSERT `Can the court set aside my earlier settlement` 10 `PHYS` TRUE FALSE `EMP` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 6 2010) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `FOUND` EQUALS `SA_OPEN`

§§ `s 50X -- what follows`

#ASSERT `Must I pay back what I received under the settlement` TRUE EQUALS `no: the agreement is void, but what you received under it cannot be recovered from you; the court may take it into account in assessing your damages (s 50X(1), (2))`
#ASSERT `Must I pay back what I received under the settlement` FALSE EQUALS `s 50X does not arise: the agreement has not been set aside under Part 7B`
